{"_id":"68df9747166b018f83df8652","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"IkN7i3ERk_lTOD0mBj3JO","description":"# Container Queries\n\nContainer Queries are a CSS feature that allows styles to be applied to an element based on the size or other characteristics of its containing element, rather than the viewport. This enables more granular and context-aware styling, where components can adapt their appearance based on the space available within their parent container, leading to more flexible and reusable designs.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"CSS container queries","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_containment/Container_queries","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144c4"},{"type":"article","title":"CSS Container Queries Guide","url":"https://css-tricks.com/css-container-queries/","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144c5"},{"type":"video","title":"Master CSS container queries and boost your web design skills!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8x8lxX5IGHY","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144c6"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-03T09:28:39.353Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa","6a20ca2fac1c5fa9928aa8d0","6a20cb82ac1c5fa9928aa8e3"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aed","68b7185fffbff9183d772aee","68b7185fffbff9183d772af0","68b7185fffbff9183d772af6","6a26960eac1c5fa9928acb63","6a26b431ac1c5fa9928acefa"],"